# oracle: pair_style snap with the quadratic C_SNAP_2021 snapcoeff and snapparam files (examples/snap), displaced lattice (2 x 2 x 2 diamond cells, 64 atoms, instead of 3 x 3 x 3: the snap force costs about 3 ms per atom per step here), velocities from atom-style variables, 25 steps of nve (was 50: the 216-atom, 50-step run took 33 s)
# oracle-potentials: C_SNAP_2021.10.15.quadratic.snapcoeff C_SNAP_2021.10.15.quadratic.snapparam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         diamond 2.845
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 12.01
variable        dx atom 0.05*sin(1.3*x+0.7*y)
variable        dy atom 0.05*cos(0.9*y-0.4*z)
variable        dz atom 0.05*sin(1.1*z+0.5*x)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.01*sin(id)
variable        vy atom 0.01*cos(2*id)
variable        vz atom 0.01*sin(3*id)
pair_style snap
pair_coeff * * C_SNAP_2021.10.15.quadratic.snapcoeff C_SNAP_2021.10.15.quadratic.snapparam C
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke press pxx pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             25
